# Cozy Bakery Website

Status: DONE
Milestone: M17 Cohesive sunlit bakery atmosphere
Dependencies: 21_WARM_BAKERY_INTERIOR.todo

## Purpose

The owner asked for the entire website to feel cozy like a bakery, with creative
decisions made autonomously. Extend the warm illustrated entrance into the page
without replacing its readable cream/green identity or authentic cake photographs.

## Tasks

- [x] Preserve affected source before extending the current interior work.
- [x] Draw an original hero window and quiet kitchen-counter footer illustration.
- [x] Add progressive cozy-bakery.css before the final readability stylesheet.
- [x] Refine header timber, paper note, linen recipe-table surround and order frame.
- [x] Keep cover faces, actual inner tabs, four-photo dialogs and all copy unchanged.
- [x] Refresh the six actual-view landscape README compositions.
- [x] Check responsive/text-zoom geometry, contrast, decoration failure and static behavior.
- [x] Run full existing site, entrance, notebook-fit and asset checks sequentially.
- [x] Publish the scoped combined interior/cozy-page result and record exact live bytes.

## Acceptance criteria

- Sunlit window artwork stays behind the real hero cake, outside the reading copy.
- Original story, contact wording, business facts and section order are unchanged.
- Cream canvas, green story/order, blush-pink covers and 48px controls remain.
- Linen and timber details do not add lines behind reading text or cake labels.
- No new motion, cream effect, generic cake cards or fabricated product photos.
- Decorative assets remain optional, noninteractive and hidden from accessibility.
- No more image-tool views; visual acceptance is not inferred from numerical checks.

